      <span class="kicker">A letter from our founder</span>
      <h3>Watching a revolution start, for the third time</h3>
      <p>In 1983, Jim Cavuoto got an early look at the first low-cost laser print engine and launched the first publication covering desktop publishing, a technology that went on to transform the printing and graphics industry. In 2001, he watched neurotech devices restore function to paralyzed patients at his alma mater and founded Neurotech Business Report, which became the publication of record for the clinical neurotech industry.</p>
      <p>At CES 2026, he saw the same early signals a third time: a wave of consumer neurotech devices ready to connect with the computers and phones people already own. BrainsConnected is his answer, built with co-founders who have grown communities and companies through two prior platform shifts. This time, the home for the wave exists before the wave crests, and you're invited in at the start.</p>
      <p class="sig">Jim Cavuoto <span>Founder and CEO, BrainsConnected</span></p>
